include "../../linux.mereo"

-- `already` BORROWS a thing that already exists, so every field is a fact about
-- that thing. Zero is not "unset": `descriptor is 0` is standard input, and this
-- program without the refusal below compiled, exited 0, and wrote its text into
-- whatever fd 0 happened to be -- silently, when fd 0 was opened read-write.
--
-- A fresh zeroed block is the OTHER job and says so: `blank linux.file`.

program goes
  msg is "borrowed nothing\n"
  t is already linux.file
  t.write (buffer is msg, count is msg.size)
end
